Carafe bench: an instruction cache invalidation reaches the JIT of every core of the process, as ic ivau and
ic iallu do on the hardware, and drops the copy of the last code page that each core keeps for decoding.
Eden invalidated only the calling core, so code that FEX writes on one core and runs on another ran from
a stale translation or was decoded from a stale copy of its page.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

